y good leadership qualities, but unfriendly, eats unhealthily. Candidate D responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner. Candidate A can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Also we have some missing info: crew cooperation, professional communication, stress resilience for A, etc.\n\nWe could respond by saying: I see strengths in Candidate C's situational awareness and leadership, which are crucial for long-distance flights, and perhaps outweigh B's interpersonal concerns. Or we could ask for more info on B's remarks. The guidelines: we should make a contribution that moves discussion forward. Perhaps we can ask for evidence on B's remarks from other panel members, and also bring up Candidate C's strengths and concerns, to compare.\n\nWe need to state our current recommendation. Could be still Candidate B, or shift to another. Let's consider: B has strong reliability and stress handling, but interpersonal remarks are concerning. C has strong situational awareness and leadership, but unfriendly and unhealthy eating (maybe not relevant). D has problem solving and responsibility but moody and loner. A has quick decisions and attention but poor communication and egocentric.\n\nWhich candidate overall best? The panel hasn't discussed C and D yet. We could argue that C's ability to anticipate dangerous situations and leadership are critical, and his unfriendly attitude may be less severe than B's nasty remarks. But we have no info on how unfriendly manifests. Could ask for more info.\n\nGiven the guidelines, we should make a focused argument. Perhaps we can say: I agree with B's strengths but need clarification on the impact of his remarks; also I want to bring up Candidate C's strong situational awareness and leadership, which are vital for long-distance flights, and ask if anyone has observed his crew cooperation. That would be a contribution.\n\nWe need to include our vote. We could keep vote as Candidate B, pending clarification. Or we could shift to Candidate C. Let's decide: I think we can keep provisional vote for Candidate B, but note that we need more info on interpersonal aspects of B and also on C's cooperation. So vote remains B.\n\nThus public message: I support B's reliability and stress handling, but ask for concrete examples of his nasty remarks and their effect; also note C's anticipation of dangerous situations and leadership, ask for crew cooperation evidence.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
